# gui/.xcode-version -- the Xcode the tracked project.pbxproj was generated on.
#
# FORMAT: marketing version, then the build version, whitespace separated.
#
# CORRECTION, 2026-08-13. Read this before trusting the pin.
#
# An earlier revision of this file claimed, as a measurement, that two Xcode
# 26.6 installs with the same xcodegen produced different bytes, and used that
# to argue the build version was the operative variable. THAT CLAIM WAS WRONG
# and it is recorded here rather than quietly deleted, because it was wrong in
# the way that matters: it was an inference presented as a measurement.
#
# Both machines were Xcode 26.6 build 17F113. Identical. The real cause was the
# CI step that installed xcodegen: it copied bin/xcodegen out of the release
# zip and left share/xcodegen/SettingPresets behind. xcodegen resolves those
# presets relative to its own location, so it silently emitted a project with
# every default build setting missing, and exited 0. Measured:
#
#   xcodegen binary alone   COMBINE_HIDPI_IMAGES occurrences: 0
#   binary + share/         COMBINE_HIDPI_IMAGES occurrences: 4
#   tracked pbxproj         COMBINE_HIDPI_IMAGES occurrences: 4
#
# So the toolchain was blamed twice, first the Xcode version and then the Xcode
# build, for a fault in how the gate installed its own generator. The gate was
# reading a broken instrument and reporting the project.
#
# WHY THE PIN STAYS, AND WHY IT KEEPS THE BUILD FIELD
#
# xcodegen does still take defaults that vary with the toolchain, so the Xcode
# that generated the tracked pbxproj is worth recording. The build version is
# kept because it identifies an Xcode exactly and costs nothing, NOT because a
# marketing-version collision was ever observed. It has not been.
#
# A mismatch here is UNAVAILABLE (exit 2), never STALE (exit 1).
26.6 17F113
